      "html": "<h3>Study question and clock</h3><p>Time to first exit-site infection after catheter placement, in months.</p><h3>Design and observation</h3><p>Kidney dialysis patients are compared by surgical versus percutaneous catheter placement.</p><p><strong>Observed information.</strong> Right-censored infection times and many tied observation times.</p><p><strong>Recorded predictors.</strong> Catheter-placement group.</p><h3>What to learn from this example</h3><p>Choose the infection definition before comparing groups. Ties affect risk-set arithmetic and Cox partial likelihood. A single constant treatment hazard ratio may miss an early-versus-late effect.</p><p>The text revisits weighted log-rank comparisons, other two-sample tests, tied-time partial likelihood, and checks of proportional hazards.</p>",
