      "html": "<h3>Study question and clock</h3><p>Age at death or departure, measured in months, for residents of Channing House.</p><h3>Design and observation</h3><p>Only people who lived long enough to enter the retirement community can be observed.</p><p><strong>Observed information.</strong> Left truncation at entry age and possible right censoring after entry.</p><p><strong>Recorded predictors.</strong> Entry age and sex; exit age and status.</p><h3>What to learn from this example</h3><p>A resident is not at risk in the observed sample before entry. Ignoring the entry requirement selects longer survivors and distorts survival estimation.</p><p>The example motivates delayed-entry risk sets, left-truncated survival estimation, male–female comparison, and proportional hazards analysis.</p>",
